1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,431
August 2003. A pizza delivery man walks
into a bank in Erie, Pennsylvania,

2
00:00:05,431 --> 00:00:08,000
with a bomb locked around his neck.

3
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:10,433
His name was Brian Wells.

4
00:00:10,433 --> 00:00:16,000
That afternoon, he took an order to
an empty TV tower site outside town.

5
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:19,798
There, a metal collar
was locked onto his neck.

6
00:00:19,798 --> 00:00:24,500
He was told to rob a bank and follow
a set of written instructions.

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,857
He walked out with about $8,700,

8
00:00:28,857 --> 00:00:32,000
and a trail of notes,
like a scavenger hunt.

9
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:34,851
Minutes later, police stopped him.

10
00:00:34,851 --> 00:00:39,000
He told them he had been forced.
They called the bomb squad.

11
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:45,441
It was still on its way when the device
went off, in front of news cameras.

12
00:00:45,441 --> 00:00:47,500
Brian Wells was 46.

13
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:49,812
The investigation took years.

14
00:00:49,812 --> 00:00:52,500
At its center was
Marjorie Diehl-Armstrong,

15
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:55,500
already tied to the death
of a former boyfriend.

16
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:58,774
Accomplice Kenneth Barnes pleaded guilty.

17
00:00:58,774 --> 00:01:03,173
In 2011, Diehl-Armstrong was
sentenced to life plus 30 years.

18
00:01:03,173 --> 00:01:05,000
She died in prison in 2017.

19
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:11,265
Whether Wells was part of the plot
or only its victim is still debated.

20
00:01:11,265 --> 00:01:15,000
What we know is that he
died waiting for help.
